  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday Night through Monday)\nIssued at 1156 PM CDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nWith the CWA on the eastern periphery of the high pressure ridge,\nanother shortwave is progged to slide southeast into the region \nTuesday night and Wednesday. Latest model solutions differ \nslightly on timing and precip details with this wave. For this \nforecast, the main potential for showers and thunderstorms looks \nto develop Tuesday night through Wednesday evening, though there \nis low potentials for precip starting as early as Tuesday late \nafternoon. With some form of the boundary still holding across \npart of the CWA and instability setting up along and south of the \nboundary, a few storms Wednesday afternoon/evening could carry \nlimited severe potential over far eastern Oklahoma and western \nArkansas. Locally damaging winds are the primary threat with hail \nbeing a secondary threat. Majority of this precip should exit with\nthe disturbance Wednesday night. \n\nFor those locations that remain dry Wednesday, continued hot and \nhumid conditions are forecast with heat index values locally above\n105 deg. Depending on how condition develop, another Heat \nAdvisory may be necessary. Once the shortwave and the boundary \ndepart the region, drier conditions and temperatures closer to \nseasonal average are anticipated Thursday and Friday. This break \nin the heat and heat stress however, look to be short-lived. \nSoutherly low level flow spreads back over the region for the \nweekend into early next week with high temperatures climbing back \ninto the upper 90s to around 103 deg over the CWA.",
